# impacket.requirements -- INPUT integrity pins for the carried impacket suite,
# the pip-native twin of arsenal.pins. build-python.sh installs these into the
# carried python's site-packages with `pip install --require-hashes --no-deps`,
# so pip refuses ANY wheel whose sha256 is not one named here -- fail-closed,
# before a byte of it is imported. --no-deps means this list is the COMPLETE
# resolved tree (21 dists), not a seed for pip to resolve further; a new
# transitive dep can never sneak in unpinned.
#
# WHY WHEELS, NOT AN sdist BUILD. impacket is pure python; its only native deps
# (pycryptodomex, cryptography, cffi, markupsafe, charset-normalizer) all ship
# prebuilt musllinux_1_2_x86_64 wheels on PyPI. so the whole suite installs with
# ZERO compilation -- pip just unpacks musl .so's into the interpreter that runs
# them. those .so ride the python tree onto xexec's exec-tmpfs (p3 is noexec; a
# separate libs dir could not be dlopen'd), so impacket lives in python/, and
# ~/tools/impacket/ carries only the pure-python runnable example scripts.
#
# to move a version: re-resolve in a musl cp312 env
#   pip download --only-binary=:all: --dest w impacket==<v> && pip hash w/*.whl
# and rewrite this file, then keep arsenal.lock in step.
#
# resolved 2026-09-14 for cpython 3.12 / musllinux_1_2_x86_64.
